(1200151, 151034, 28141, '<td valign="top">Billboards need to be simple to draw all attention to the product - remember most billboards are targeted at people who are busy driving.  The table cloth and background texture are too distracting.</td>', 'Billboards need to be simple to draw all attention to the product - remember most billboards are targeted at people who are busy driving.  The table cloth and background texture are too distracting.', '2005-02-28 22:18:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200152, 150390, 28141, '<td valign="top">Trees in background are too distracting.  The man needs to stick out from the background to make him an effective advertising tool.</td>', 'Trees in background are too distracting.  The man needs to stick out from the background to make him an effective advertising tool.', '2005-02-28 22:20:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200153, 150937, 10080, '<td valign="top">Very nice! If I  could suggest one thing, it would be to dodge that grey part behind the butterfly to white, and make him(or her) jump out at you. Still a very nice capture. 8</td>', 'Very nice! If I  could suggest one thing, it would be to dodge that grey part behind the butterfly to white, and make him(or her) jump out at you. Still a very nice capture. 8', '2005-02-28 22:20:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200154, 150837, 28141, '<td valign="top">The challenge was to take a photo that could serve as a billboard advertisement, not to take a photo of an existing billboard.</td>', 'The challenge was to take a photo that could serve as a billboard advertisement, not to take a photo of an existing billboard.', '2005-02-28 22:21:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200157, 150871, 28141, '<td valign="top">Needs better focus/sharpening.   The pixelation in the shadowed skintones is really distracting.</td>', 'Needs better focus/sharpening.   The pixelation in the shadowed skintones is really distracting.', '2005-02-28 22:22:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200160, 150719, 28141, '<td valign="top">The smokestack is too small and the clouds it is creating don''t stand out quite enough.  Remember, billboards are generally viewed by people busy driving.  Subjects need to be large and stand out from the background so that the viewer can pick them out instantly.</td>', 'The smokestack is too small and the clouds it is creating don''t stand out quite enough.  Remember, billboards are generally viewed by people busy driving.  Subjects need to be large and stand out from the background so that the viewer can pick them out instantly.', '2005-02-28 22:24:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200162, 150930, 28141, '<td valign="top">Cute, but it''s difficult to see the details (i.e. the legs).  Remember, most billboard viewers are distracted drivers who have only a second to take in the image.</td>', 'Cute, but it''s difficult to see the details (i.e. the legs).  Remember, most billboard viewers are distracted drivers who have only a second to take in the image.', '2005-02-28 22:25:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200166, 151092, 28141, '<td valign="top">I''d like to see this with a larger depth of field, such that his ear is in focus.</td>', 'I''d like to see this with a larger depth of field, such that his ear is in focus.', '2005-02-28 22:27:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200172, 150959, 28141, '<td valign="top">Perhaps my moniter is calibrated too bright, but it''s very difficult to see the string.</td>', 'Perhaps my moniter is calibrated too bright, but it''s very difficult to see the string.', '2005-02-28 22:28:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200179, 150614, 28141, '<td valign="top">The fox is too hard to pick out.  Remember, the target audience of most billboards is distracted drivers who only have a second to view the image.  They need to be able to pick out the subject and read the message quickley.</td>', 'The fox is too hard to pick out.  Remember, the target audience of most billboards is distracted drivers who only have a second to view the image.  They need to be able to pick out the subject and read the message quickley.', '2005-02-28 22:34:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200182, 150591, 28141, '<td valign="top">Looks very much like all the real ipod ads.  The edges need to be sharper though.</td>', 'Looks very much like all the real ipod ads.  The edges need to be sharper though.', '2005-02-28 22:35:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200187, 151023, 28141, '<td valign="top">Yay Oregon!  (my childhood home)  Beautiful shot, but perhaps a tighter frame might be better so the person would be larger.  They might be hard for a distracted driver to pick out at this size.</td>', 'Yay Oregon!  (my childhood home)  Beautiful shot, but perhaps a tighter frame might be better so the person would be larger.  They might be hard for a distracted driver to pick out at this size.', '2005-02-28 22:39:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200212, 150996, 13119, '<td valign="top">Isnt this already a billboard that you just took a picture of?</td>', 'Isnt this already a billboard that you just took a picture of?', '2005-02-28 22:52:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200219, 150559, 23394, '<td valign="top">ok, i am voting this challenge in 2 passes.  in this pass, you will get a partial comment and a score.  then i will come back to comment again.  if you have any problem whatsoever with this comment, pm me and let me know.  otherwise, take it with a grain of salt...i''m not trying to be a know-it-all, i''m just explaining where i''m coming from in voting this challenge.  and, if this comment is NOT helpful (of if you think i''m full of $#!+), don''t mark it helpful.<br/> <br/>billboards are a science unto themselves.  a <i>lot</i> of research has gone into determining just how much information a person can digest <i>and retain</i> in specific time spans.  they use this information to develop formulas for determining the number of words and letters to use on billboards, as well as their sizes.  they also determine the size and number of visual elements to include.<br/> <br/>the graphics/photograph on a billboard are designed to get the point across in a moment.  on the road, a driver will have less time with a billboard than a voter will give your image.  this is a key element in the challenge:  composing a shot that will get its point across quickly and succintly.  along those lines, a strong composition will probably have few details and make strong use of negative space.<br/>----------------<br/>what a gut-wrenching concept!  i hope you''re not getting too beaten up for the size; you really could have cropped off the top without diminishing the impact of the idea.  very evocative.  not necessarily the best photograph, but at 60 mph, people aren''t usually looking at the details...good luck!</td>', 'ok, i am voting this challenge in 2 passes.  in this pass, you will get a partial comment and a score.  then i will come back to comment again.  if you have any problem whatsoever with this comment, pm me and let me know.  otherwise, take it with a grain of salt...i''m not trying to be a know-it-all, i''m just explaining where i''m coming from in voting this challenge.  and, if this comment is NOT helpful (of if you think i''m full of $#!+), don''t mark it helpful. billboards are a science unto themselves.  a lot of research has gone into determining just how much information a person can digest and retain in specific time spans.  they use this information to develop formulas for determining the number of words and letters to use on billboards, as well as their sizes.  they also determine the size and number of visual elements to include. the graphics/photograph on a billboard are designed to get the point across in a moment.  on the road, a driver will have less time with a billboard than a voter will give your image.  this is a key element in the challenge:  composing a shot that will get its point across quickly and succintly.  along those lines, a strong composition will probably have few details and make strong use of negative space.----------------what a gut-wrenching concept!  i hope you''re not getting too beaten up for the size; you really could have cropped off the top without diminishing the impact of the idea.  very evocative.  not necessarily the best photograph, but at 60 mph, people aren''t usually looking at the details...good luck!', '2005-02-28 22:56:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1200223, 150798, 23394, '<td valign="top">ok, i am voting this challenge in 2 passes.  in this pass, you will get a partial comment and a score.  then i will come back to comment again.  if you have any problem whatsoever with this comment, pm me and let me know.  otherwise, take it with a grain of salt...i''m not trying to be a know-it-all, i''m just explaining where i''m coming from in voting this challenge.  and, if this comment is NOT helpful (of if you think i''m full of $#!+), don''t mark it helpful.<br/> <br/>billboards are a science unto themselves.  a <i>lot</i> of research has gone into determining just how much information a person can digest <i>and retain</i> in specific time spans.  they use this information to develop formulas for determining the number of words and letters to use on billboards, as well as their sizes.  they also determine the size and number of visual elements to include.<br/> <br/>the graphics/photograph on a billboard are designed to get the point across in a moment.  on the road, a driver will have less time with a billboard than a voter will give your image.  this is a key element in the challenge:  composing a shot that will get its point across quickly and succintly.  along those lines, a strong composition will probably have few details and make strong use of negative space.<br/>----------<br/>nice concept.  works well as a photograph, almost as well as a billboard.  in terms of imagery and conveying the idea, you nailed it.  the presentation is off, though, due to the border.  the toe tag could have been a bit heavier, as it would be hard to read at 60 mph.  all the same, one of the better entries in the challenge.  good luck!</td>', 'ok, i am voting this challenge in 2 passes.  in this pass, you will get a partial comment and a score.  then i will come back to comment again.  if you have any problem whatsoever with this comment, pm me and let me know.  otherwise, take it with a grain of salt...i''m not trying to be a know-it-all, i''m just explaining where i''m coming from in voting this challenge.  and, if this comment is NOT helpful (of if you think i''m full of $#!+), don''t mark it helpful. billboards are a science unto themselves.  a lot of research has gone into determining just how much information a person can digest and retain in specific time spans.  they use this information to develop formulas for determining the number of words and letters to use on billboards, as well as their sizes.  they also determine the size and number of visual elements to include. the graphics/photograph on a billboard are designed to get the point across in a moment.  on the road, a driver will have less time with a billboard than a voter will give your image.  this is a key element in the challenge:  composing a shot that will get its point across quickly and succintly.  along those lines, a strong composition will probably have few details and make strong use of negative space.----------nice concept.  works well as a photograph, almost as well as a billboard.  in terms of imagery and conveying the idea, you nailed it.  the presentation is off, though, due to the border.  the toe tag could have been a bit heavier, as it would be hard to read at 60 mph.  all the same, one of the better entries in the challenge.  good luck!', '2005-02-28 22:59:45.000000', NULL, 1),
