you think i''m full of $#!+), don''t mark it helpful. billboards are a science unto themselves.  a lot of research has gone into determining just how much information a person can digest and retain in specific time spans.  they use this information to develop formulas for determining the number of words and letters to use on billboards, as well as their sizes.  they also determine the size and number of visual elements to include. the graphics/photograph on a billboard are designed to get the point across in a moment.  on the road, a driver will have less time with a billboard than a voter will give your image.  this is a key element in the challenge:  composing a shot that will get its point across quickly and succintly.  along those lines, a strong composition will probably have few details and make strong use of negative space.----------------what an image!  nicely seen and composed.  i am sure you went out on this climb just for this challenge.  as for the challenge, i think this definitely works, and i hope to see it on the front page.  good luck!', '2005-03-04 04:52:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1207344, 150495, 25655, '<td valign="top">My evaluation method of this challenge is as follows:<br/>1. Did you catch my eye while I was driving by?  Yes<br/>2. If I didn''t catch the text while I was driving, did you intrigue me enough to look for this billboard again? No words needed<br/>3. Did you sell your stuff to me? Yes<br/>4. Extra thoughts:  Coke... the cornyest idea ever. It sells itself. You don''t need to work too hard.<br/>This is not something that will be taken off your score though. Not to worry :-) <br/>This is a nice billboard. I like the crop that reveals only part of the bottles. The soft focus make them look very cold and wet. Works wonderfully when I''m thirsty.<br/>I think I would like this one better if you had cloned out the little dark spots of dirt from the white text on the box and crop a bit tighter on both sides. (6)</td>', 'My evaluation method of this challenge is as follows:1. Did you catch my eye while I was driving by?  Yes2. If I didn''t catch the text while I was driving, did you intrigue me enough to look for this billboard again? No words needed3. Did you sell your stuff to me? Yes4. Extra thoughts:  Coke... the cornyest idea ever. It sells itself. You don''t need to work too hard.This is not something that will be taken off your score though. Not to worry :-) This is a nice billboard. I like the crop that reveals only part of the bottles. The soft focus make them look very cold and wet. Works wonderfully when I''m thirsty.I think I would like this one better if you had cloned out the little dark spots of dirt from the white text on the box and crop a bit tighter on both sides. (6)', '2005-03-04 10:11:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1207350, 150978, 25655, '<td valign="top">My evaluation method of this challenge is as follows:<br/>1. Did you catch my eye while I was driving by?  Yes<br/>2. If I didn''t catch the text while I was driving, did you intrigue me enough to look for this billboard again? No words needed<br/>3. Did you sell your stuff to me? Yes<br/>4. Extra thoughts:  Many absolutes here today :-)<br/>A product that sells itself easily. All you need is to keep the clean look, which I think you kept nicely.<br/>I wish I could see the titles on the bottle better. Some contrast would not hurt here.<br/>I am also bumping up for being validated! (7)</td>', 'My evaluation method of this challenge is as follows:1. Did you catch my eye while I was driving by?  Yes2. If I didn''t catch the text while I was driving, did you intrigue me enough to look for this billboard again? No words needed3. Did you sell your stuff to me? Yes4. Extra thoughts:  Many absolutes here today :-)A product that sells itself easily. All you need is to keep the clean look, which I think you kept nicely.I wish I could see the titles on the bottle better. Some contrast would not hurt here.I am also bumping up for being validated! (7)', '2005-03-04 10:13:32.000000', NULL, 1),
