(1209333, 150584, 93, '<td valign="top">How did you add the text? You obviously didn''t do it digitally.. printed it out on the background?  Actually, given the reflection in the glass, It looks like that''s exactly what you did.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-05 12:46:18.</i></td>', 'How did you add the text? You obviously didn''t do it digitally.. printed it out on the background?  Actually, given the reflection in the glass, It looks like that''s exactly what you did.', '2005-03-05 12:45:48.000000', '2005-03-05 12:46:18.000000', 0),
(1209389, 150798, 2022, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a well deserved ribbon ! Great idea, great picture !</td>', 'Congratulations on a well deserved ribbon ! Great idea, great picture !', '2005-03-05 13:37:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1209391, 150630, 2022, '<td valign="top">I am so glad this one ribboned, I voted 10 for it. Congratulations !</td>', 'I am so glad this one ribboned, I voted 10 for it. Congratulations !', '2005-03-05 13:37:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1209394, 151023, 2022, '<td valign="top">Congrats ! Job well done !</td>', 'Congrats ! Job well done !', '2005-03-05 13:40:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1209426, 151023, 16230, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all of you for the nice comments. Even though many of them were directed to Zoomdak (we both had a good laugh over that), it''s still very nice to get so much positive feedback. It''s also very nice to win a ribbon. I can feel my head expanding already! :)<br/> <br/>FYI, I did not set out to fool anyone by doing a ''Zoomdak'' photo. It just sort of worked out that way. I did take this photo on Cannon Beach, but I didn''t go anywhere near Haystack Rock (Zoomdak Rock?). There were so many people around Haystack at the time that I doubt I could have gotten close enough to take a photo. It''s a very popular place. I originally planned to do a Toyota billboard using a photo of my new Tundra parked on the beach with the sunset in the background. But the closest place that I know of where you can drive onto the sand was too far away for us to make it that day. So we stopped by Cannon Beach instead.<br/> <br/>I gladly admit that Zoomdak''s excellent photos of Haystack Rock did influence some of my decisions while taking this photo; and in the post-shot editing too. He is a very talented young man, and I have no doubt that we''ll be seeing even more ribbons on his profile page in the future. I just wonder who I''ll have to be to win my next ribbon. So, how far is Iceland from Oregon? :)<br/></td>', 'Thanks to all of you for the nice comments. Even though many of them were directed to Zoomdak (we both had a good laugh over that), it''s still very nice to get so much positive feedback. It''s also very nice to win a ribbon. I can feel my head expanding already! :) FYI, I did not set out to fool anyone by doing a ''Zoomdak'' photo. It just sort of worked out that way. I did take this photo on Cannon Beach, but I didn''t go anywhere near Haystack Rock (Zoomdak Rock?). There were so many people around Haystack at the time that I doubt I could have gotten close enough to take a photo. It''s a very popular place. I originally planned to do a Toyota billboard using a photo of my new Tundra parked on the beach with the sunset in the background. But the closest place that I know of where you can drive onto the sand was too far away for us to make it that day. So we stopped by Cannon Beach instead. I gladly admit that Zoomdak''s excellent photos of Haystack Rock did influence some of my decisions while taking this photo; and in the post-shot editing too. He is a very talented young man, and I have no doubt that we''ll be seeing even more ribbons on his profile page in the future. I just wonder who I''ll have to be to win my next ribbon. So, how far is Iceland from Oregon? :)', '2005-03-05 14:03:35.000000', NULL, 0),
